    observe: "Luke 15:7 says there will be more joy in heaven over one sinner who repents than over ninety-nine righteous persons who need no repentance. In verse 20 the father saw the son 'while he was still far off', felt compassion, ran and embraced and kissed him. The son began his prepared speech, but the father interrupted, calling for the best robe, a ring, sandals and a feast. The story ends with the father pleading with the older son, 'You are always with me, and all that is mine is yours.'",
